    "narrative": "At Arzúa the Camino del Norte ends. The yellow arrows merge with the arrows of the Camino Francés and from here the two routes are one. The density of walkers triples in a single afternoon. Pilgrims who have come from Ferrol on the Inglés, from Oviedo on the Primitivo, from Irún on the Norte, from St. Jean Pied de Port on the Francés — all arrive in Arzúa within days of each other. The cafés are crowded. The albergues fill by 14:00. It can feel overwhelming after thirty quiet days on the Norte. But this is the old shape of the Camino: many rivers into one. From Arzúa it is two days to Santiago on the shared path (19.3 km to O Pedrouzo, then 19.4 km to Santiago), documented in routes/camino-frances/stages.json stages 31-32. The Norte proper ends here, at the junction.",
